    <summary type="text">the Logos web app is DISGUSTINGY bright/white - enough to actually ruin your morning...</summary>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;the Logos web app is DISGUSTINGY bright/white - enough to actually ruin your morning&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thankfully there&amp;rsquo;s an extension called &lt;a href=&#34;https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/styl-us/&#34;&gt;stylus&lt;/a&gt; and some &lt;a href=&#34;/kind/&#34; class=&#34;glossary-term&#34; title=&#34;kind - kubernetes in docker&#34; data-hover-title=&#34;kind&#34;&gt;kind&lt;/a&gt; folks in the Logos community created a nice dark theme &lt;a href=&#34;https://userstyles.world/style/18547/logos-web-app-dark-mode&#34;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. You simply install the extension, then go to the userstyles link &amp;lt;&amp;ndash; and click &lt;code&gt;install&lt;/code&gt;. It only changes themes for the sites configured - in this case &lt;a href=&#34;app.logos.com&#34;&gt;app.logos.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;todo-image&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;heading-wear-glyph&#34;&gt;TODO: image&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;</content>
